  "about": "Tenshu Calendar's store-screenshot fixture (docs/how-to/store-screenshots.md §3b): one invented person's calendars — work, family, fitness, a trip — generated at run time by store/fixtures/calendar/generate_calendar.py as one .ics file per calendar, which Calendar's -seedFixture launch imports through the same importIcs call the calendar row's Import or export… sheet makes. Nobody here is real. Every date is relative to the day of the run: `day` counts calendar days from today, `workday` counts weekdays (0 = today, or the next Monday at a weekend), `weekday` + `week` is that weekday in the week `week` weeks from this one (weeks start on Sunday, as the US region the run uses does). A `repeat` starts five weeks back, so the month grid is full on both sides of today. Times are floating (no TZID), so they read the same in any simulator time zone. `default: true` is the calendar the app seeds itself on first launch (Personal); the seed imports into it rather than creating it.",
